   "kind": "attr",
   "tier": "detail",
   "quote": "secret names",
   "select": "outs",
   "cond": {
    "path": "value",
    "op": "contains",
    "value": "protein-engineering/cognito/client-secret"
   }
  },
  {
   "id": "out_param_names",
   "kind": "any_of",
   "tier": "detail",
   "quote": "parameter and secret names as stack outputs",
   "checks": [
    {
     "kind": "attr",
     "select": "outs",
     "cond": {
      "path": "value",
      "op": "regex",
      "value": "^/protein-agent/cognito/"
     }
    },
    {
     "kind": "ref",
     "from": "outs",
     "to": "ssm"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "project_param",
   "kind": "attr",
   "tier": "detail",
   "quote": "for a project named \"protein-engineering\" by default",
   "select": {
    "types": [
     "__parameter__"
    ]
   },
   "cond": {
    "path": "default",
    "op": "eq",
    "value": "protein-engineering"
   }
  },
  {
   "id": "x_oauth_enabled",
   "kind": "attr",
   "tier": "extra",
   "select": "client",
   "cond": {
    "path": "AllowedOAuthFlowsUserPoolClient",
    "op": "eq",
    "value": "true"
   }
  },
  {
   "id": "x_idp",
   "kind": "attr",
   "tier": "extra",
   "select": "client",
   "cond": {
    "path": "SupportedIdentityProviders.*",
    "op": "eq",
    "value": "COGNITO"
   }
  },
  {
   "id": "x_prevent",
   "kind": "attr",
   "tier": "extra",
   "select": "client",
   "cond": {
    "path": "PreventUserExistenceErrors",
    "op": "eq",
    "value": "ENABLED"
   }
  }
 ],
 "notes": "Execution role matched by its Lambda trust, not by name. The hosted-domain prefix is checked only for the region name (adapter value us-east-1); the stack-ID fragment renders as an opaque placeholder and is not checked. The custom resource is selected via __declared__ because Custom::<Name> types cannot be listed; a gated custom resource would also match. The symbols parameter is matched by name (symbol/special) because Ref to a parameter resolves to its default, so the link from RequireSymbols is not observable. 'Updating it on stack updates' is not checked: handlers commonly treat every non-Delete request as create-or-update without naming 'Update', so no code pattern separates compliant from non-compliant handlers."
}